  "assumptions": [
    "Configured model: deterministic-fallback; adjustment mode: deterministic.",
    "Model text is not used as factual rationale; physics results govern status.",
    "Line installation is fixed at the first planning condition water level (1.8 ft MLLW); no implicit tending between conditions.",
    "Forecast-only planning checks the supplied conditions; it does not establish MST design-condition compliance. Intake selects representative snapshots, not every forecast sample; use the forecast-plan endpoint for an arrival/holding interval assessment.",
    "Quasi-static 3-DOF equilibrium (surge, sway, yaw) of a rigid hull; heave, roll, pitch and dynamics are not modeled.",
    "Applied environmental loads include wind and current only; wave and wake loads are not evaluated.",
    "Lines are tension-only; tension = parts x effective MBS x curve(strain) with the catalog stretch curve scaled by the effective (wet/dry) MBS.",
    "Fenders are unilateral springs (catalog linear stiffness) in contact over a parallel body of +/- half the waterline length.",
    "Pier-fitting loads are the 3-D vector sum of attached lines compared with the nominal capacity.",
    "Rest lengths are set at the installation water level and stay fixed; the ship rides the water level.",
    "Design factor 3.0 (MST II).",
    "line 1: rest length from default 2% pretension.",
    "line 2: rest length from default 2% pretension.",
    "line 3: rest length from default 2% pretension.",
    "line 4: rest length from default 2% pretension.",
    "line 5: rest length from default 2% pretension.",
    "line 6: rest length from default 2% pretension.",
    "Gust duration not given: assumed 30 s (legacy).",
    "Wind averaging/gust duration/height not documented in the snapshot: legacy assumption applied (10 m, 60 s sustained, 30 s gust).",
    "No lines fast: tugs must cancel the whole static wind-and-current wrench (surge, sway, yaw) at the berthing heading.",
    "Catalog bollard pull (seed/estimated unless published); ahead for pushing, astern for pulling, capped by the push point rating; efficiency factor 1. Not certified ratings. Horsepower is not converted to force.",
    "Margin 25% applied to the wrench.",
    "UFC 4-159-03 (2020), Chapter 4; Eq. 4-3 harmonic and symmetric angle folding restored from the earlier UFC edition.",
    "Wind basis follows supplied metadata; unsupported conversions and any legacy assumptions are listed below.",
    "Wind shielding scales all wind forces and moments equally; current is unshielded.",
    "Static wind and current loads only; wave and wake loads are not evaluated.",
    "Water depth is actual depth at the ship; water level is not added again.",
    "Current model assumes a wide harbor/channel, level keel, and 15 C salt-water viscosity (Table 4-1); density uses the request.",
    "Yaw uses UFC Tables 4-5/4-10: DDG and CG use destroyer wind / FFG current; CVN and LHD use carrier wind / CVE 55 current. CG is assumed at midships.",
    "Ship geometry is estimated: Wind-force magnitudes calibrated to NSTM Table 582-3-1 with areas within 25% of original seeds; peak bearings also match after converting NSTM flow-toward angles to API wind-from angles. Transverse drag class is extensive_superstructure (C=1.02), per UFC Table 4-2 for destroyers. Dimensions approximate from public fact sheets; fittings notional. Superstructure height frozen before area calibration using original hull area/LWL plus original superstructure area/(0.5 LWL), assuming a rectangular half-length superstructure. Midship coefficient 0.83 estimated by analogy to UFC Table 4-8 destroyer. Wetted surface estimated with UFC Eq. 4-18 at full_load and density 1020 kg/m3; other loadings recompute the estimate. Propeller expanded area estimated using Eqs. 4-22/4-23 and Table 4-7, pitch ratio 1 (LHD uses carrier analogy).",
    "Line installation tide: 1.8 ft MLLW; no implicit tending in these draft static checks.",
    "Loading full_load; strength design factor uses MST II.",
    "Intermediate states: only deployed parts are modeled (one until double_up), slack until taken to power; tugs hold until every line is on its bollard. Tug release is checked before further tensioning.",
    "Static check only: transient loads while lines are handled and tugs maneuver are not evaluated; they need the M11 simulator.",
    "Rule table is a draft from NSTM 582-2.4.6 paragraph references that were not re-verified in this repository.",
    "Durations are unreviewed planning estimates, not measured line-handling times.",
    "200 instantaneous samples of gust factor, direction and current from model 'synthetic-demo' r1; each solved to equilibrium.",
    "Failed samples are counted, reported and used to bound the probability.",
    "Fender exceedance compares energy with rated energy; reported load percentiles are reaction force in lbf.",
    "No dynamic or snatch amplification is modeled; the dynamic factor, if any, scales wind force once."
